SyncUps instrumentation patch for the MSc benchmark.
Origin: original, 
Upstream: https://github.com/pointfreeco/syncups @ 170bc1ad7b0ec1e64606d7c45c54456a0f26b04c (main)

Apply (from the repo root):
  git clone https://github.com/pointfreeco/syncups apps/external/syncups
  git -C apps/external/syncups checkout 170bc1ad7b0ec1e64606d7c45c54456a0f26b04c
  cp apps/external/syncups-Instrumentation.swift apps/external/syncups/SyncUps/Instrumentation.swift
  git -C apps/external/syncups apply ../syncups.patch
Build (no -sdk flag: it would build the Swift macro plugins for the simulator instead of the Mac):
  xcodebuild -project SyncUps.xcodeproj -scheme SyncUps -configuration Debug \
    -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17,OS=27.0' -derivedDataPath build \
    -skipMacroValidation -skipPackagePluginValidation CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build

Contents:
  Instrumentation (benchmark, D-019; spec docs/external-perturbations.md):
    Instrumentation.swift: Perturb enum (8 flags su01..su08), UnlabelledSymbol (copied from the testbed),
      optionalIdentifier, ResetData seed.
    SyncUpsApp.swift: ResetData.applyIfRequested().
    SyncUpsList.swift: su01 Add icon, su03 notes flag passed to the new form, su05 confirm label,
      su04 theme caption and su06 generic row label (CardView).
    SyncUpForm.swift: su03 Notes section (new form only), su07 icon-only Theme row (edit sheet only;
      a Menu with an inline Picker, because a Picker borrows "Paint Palette" from the selected option).
    SyncUpDetail.swift: baseline id editSyncUpButton (removed by su02), su07 passed to the edit sheet,
      su08 icon-only Delete.
    project.pbxproj adds Instrumentation.swift to the SyncUps target.
  Build compatibility with Xcode 27.1 / iOS 27 SDK (not instrumentation):
    RecordMeeting.swift: SpeakerArc marked nonisolated (target defaults to MainActor, Shape is nonisolated).
    Package.resolved: swift-sharing 2.8.0 -> 2.8.2 (2.8.0 fails to link with Swift 6.4; within the
    project's own "up to next major from 2.0.0" requirement).

